{"id": "EUVD-2026-102273", "enisaUuid": "a746fe89-b843-3f0a-8057-041b0e2cc806", "description": "ytnef through 2.1.2 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in MAPIPrint() that allows attackers to read past heap allocations by supplying compressed RTF properties. Attackers can deliver a crafted winmail.dat whose decompressed RTF lacks a NUL terminator, causing printf to over-read, crashing ytnefprint and leaking adjacent heap bytes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:45:21", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/ytnef-decompressrtf-oob-read", "https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef/issues/112", "https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef/blob/d9f089144414d3b0912c29ab96f8f1c591d00319/lib/ytnef.c#L1449-L1458", "https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef/blob/d9f089144414d3b0912c29ab96f8f1c591d00319/lib/ytnef.c#L1605-L1614", "https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ytnef-through-2.1.2-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-mapiprint-in-lib-ytnef-c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111146", "GHSA-j8vr-p842-7vj8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "dc950af3-6d44-3b0b-920d-6f92dae7acc8", "product": {"name": "ytnef", "vendor": {"name": "ytnef"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.1.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "950f7055-03de-30ef-b5c2-30583409a950", "vendor": {"name": "Yeraze"}}], "isExploited": false}